{"name":"Desert Hot Springs","hex":"#c4c8aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Desert Hot Springs","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Riverside County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Desert_Hot_Springs"}],"entries":[{"title":"Desert Hot Springs (thermal mineral springs)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert Hot Springs is a geothermal geographic area in Riverside County, California with several hot springs. Since 1941, the California Department of Conservation has recorded approximately 200 geothermal wells that have been drilled in this geographic area; approximately 50 of which are used for commercial spas and pools."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Desert_Hot_Springs_2008.jpg/330px-Desert_Hot_Springs_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_Hot_Springs_(thermal_mineral_springs)","wikidata":"Q86762204"},{"title":"Desert Hot Springs, California","blocks":[{"text":"Desert Hot Springs is a city in Riverside County, California, United States. The city is located within the Coachella Valley geographic region. The population was 32,512 as of the 2020 census, up from 25,938 at the 2010 census. The city has experienced rapid growth since the 1970s when there were 2,700 residents. The city is commonly referred to by its initials, DHS."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Desert_Hot_Springs%2C_California_City_Hall.jpg/330px-Desert_Hot_Springs%2C_California_City_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_Hot_Springs%2C_California","wikidata":"Q573096"},{"title":"Hot spring","blocks":[{"text":"A hot spring, thermal spring, hydrothermal spring, or geothermal spring is a spring produced by the emergence of geothermally heated groundwater onto the surface of the Earth. The groundwater is heated either by shallow bodies of magma or by circulation through faults to hot rock deep in the Earth's crust."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Aerial_view_of_Grand_Prismatic_%2823428929375%29.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_Grand_Prismatic_%2823428929375%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_spring","wikidata":"Q177380"},{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert","wikidata":"Q8514"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/This_Natural_Hot_Mineral_Water_Pool_is_maintained_at_about_95_degrees_with_a_constant_flow_of_approximately_125_gallons_a_minute_%2880818%29.jpg/500px-This_Natural_Hot_Mineral_Water_Pool_is_maintained_at_about_95_degrees_with_a_constant_flow_of_approximately_125_gallons_a_minute_%2880818%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/This_Natural_Hot_Mineral_Water_Pool_is_maintained_at_about_95_degrees_with_a_constant_flow_of_approximately_125_gallons_a_minute_%2880818%29.jpg/1280px-Th